WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:04.600
Third question that came in this week, how
likely is it that any president is really

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.320
going to pack the court and add seats to the
Supreme Court?

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.990
So this is an interesting question, because
this is often mentioned when anytime we talk

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:18.020
about the Supreme Court, invariably the question
comes up about, you know, if Mitch McConnell

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.870
is going to hold the seat for a year.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:26.350
So Barack Obama can't put in Merrick Garland
and Donald Trump gets to put a Neil Gorsuch

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:31.510
next time there's a Democratic president,
that person, he or she should just add seats

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:34.820
to the Supreme Court, because you can do that.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:40.019
And that way, you know, if it ends up being
seven two, you just add a bunch of justices

00:00:40.019 --> 00:00:44.170
and all of a sudden you've got a left leaning
majority.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.600
I think that the risk of doing it.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:54.050
And the reason it's not been done recently
is that if a Democratic president were to

00:00:54.050 --> 00:01:01.089
add seats to the Supreme Court and, for example,
Republicans still control the Senate, Republicans

00:01:01.089 --> 00:01:06.820
can hold up the confirmations of all of the
lower court appointees.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.410
Most cases never make it to the Supreme Court.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:13.860
And the lower court just judges are extremely
important.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:19.300
And you could potentially fuel, number one,
Republicans just obstructing every single

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.300
one of your actual selections.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:26.120
And number two, every time we have a new president,
they're going to add seats to the Supreme

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:27.120
Court.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.050
I just don't know that that's the right way
to go.

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:32.810
There's things that need to be changed, for
example.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:36.930
There should not have been a mechanism for
Mitch McConnell to hold the seat open that

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:42.210
could have been filled by Merrick Garland,
filled with Merrick Garland by Barack Obama

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.320
for a year.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.500
It just shouldn't be allowed to do that.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.550
There should be, you know, some some process.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:51.780
And you can think of 10 different ways that
it could be done where that's not possible.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:56.340
We could potentially be looking at ending
lifetime appointments for Supreme Court justices.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:59.540
Now, I know that there are good arguments
on both sides.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:05.010
One of them being, if a Supreme Court justice
is to be truly independent, they must not

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:13.380
have on their minds, even subconsciously,
the possibility that they may work in an industry

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:17.670
after they are out of the Supreme Court where
they are adjudicating a case.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.390
And that may be a factor in how I get that.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:26.450
But there's probably ways to deal with that,
which would solve the issue of lifetime appointments

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:32.290
where you're essentially waiting for people
to die or to be so elderly that they can't

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:33.870
do the job anymore.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:37.540
And the timing of it means it's a very ugly
system in a sense.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:41.260
So I don't you know, I know that it's discussed
quite a bit.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:46.340
I don't expect Donald Trump to pack the Supreme
Court if he wins a second term.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:51.200
I don't expect Joe Biden to add Supreme Court
justices if he were to defeat Donald Trump

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.330
in November.

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:56.350
It's a fraught and complicated issue that
requires more exploration.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:59.930
But I do think there are other changes that
should be made to the Supreme Court that would

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:04.069
not necessarily lead to this just persistent
race to the bottom, a race to the top, where

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:09.200
every time you get a new president, they say,
let's add two and I'll select them.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.190
And of course, again, if you don't have control
of the Senate.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:17.400
The other party could block your selections
to those new seats as well, so complicated

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.400
issue.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.530
I would love to hear your thoughts on it.

